<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vishnugopa of Kanchi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vishnugopa of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchi</a> was a Pallava king of Kanchipuram in the mid-4th century. He is named in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prayagraj">Allahabad</a> pillar inscription of the Gupta emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samudragupta">Samudragupta</a> among the southern kings who were defeated and then reinstated during Samudragupta's southern campaign, which makes him one of the earliest Pallava rulers whose date is fixed.</p></div>
